Z||000000||MontanaFiero||10-03-2001||04:00 AM||||Does anyone know if the Fiero Power Door Lock system uses a relay anywhere in the circuit? I am getting ready to install Remote Keyless Entry and wiring it is different with - or - without relays. <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||10-03-2001||07:02 AM||||Yep- relays||||reg||1
Z||000002||SKIDMARK||10-03-2001||09:26 AM||||I believe the relays are in a block under the passenger side front speaker. That's where the horn relay is anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000003||gomobile||10-03-2001||09:51 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MontanaFiero:<BR><B>Does anyone know if the Fiero Power Door Lock system uses a relay anywhere in the circuit? I am getting ready to install Remote Keyless Entry and wiring it is different with - or - without relays. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Let me know how it comes out as I am also thinking of doing the same thing. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bill Osmer||10-03-2001||01:48 PM||||Most after market alarms & keyless entry systmes have good instructions for installation - mine did (Bulldog brand). I tapped into the existing power door lock switch wires in the kick panel of the driver's door. Use a manual w/wiring diagrams to identify wire colors. This method taps right into using the OE relay system. End result - works great!!<P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000005||normalicy||10-05-2001||07:23 PM||||All GMs definitely have relays (unless from Japan).  Best way to hook up power door locks is to follow what Bill Osmer suggested by going to the drivers kick panel where all the wires are.  The ones you need are going to be blue and white/black if I remember correctly.  Check by putting a test light on the wire (ground the other end).  If they are negative trip, they will try to lock/unlock.  If not, then all you have to do is push the lock/unlock button and if the light lights up, then you know that it is one of the wires you need.<P>That should be about it.<P>------------------<BR>What is normal anyway?||||reg||1
